    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Question\n\nHi,\r\n\r\ncurrently I'am trying to migrate from luasnip to mini.snippets. On testing I stumbled upon the issue that `LINE_COMMENT` for PHP uses the block comment string (`/*`) in stead of the line comment string (`//`). [see](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a03a9a4f79916579b2debaec629333e2ebdd82b5/lua/mini/snippets.lua#L2041)\r\n```\r\n:lua print(vim.bo.commentstring:gsub('%s*%%s.*$', ''))\r\n```\r\nindeed gives `/*`, but in luasnip `LINE_COMMENT` did give `//`.\r\n\r\nIs there a way to set this comment string in mini.snippet for a specific language  of is this a bug?\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.snippets</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">currently I'am trying to migrate from luasnip to mini.snippets. On testing I stumbled upon the issue that <code class=\"notranslate\">LINE_COMMENT</code> for PHP uses the block comment string (<code class=\"notranslate\">/*</code>) in stead of the line comment string (<code class=\"notranslate\">//</code>). <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a03a9a4f79916579b2debaec629333e2ebdd82b5/lua/mini/snippets.lua#L2041\">see</a></p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\":lua print(vim.bo.commentstring:gsub('%s*%%s.*$', ''))\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">:lua print(vim.bo.commentstring:gsub('%s*%%s.*$', ''))\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">indeed gives <code class=\"notranslate\">/*</code>, but in luasnip <code class=\"notranslate\">LINE_COMMENT</code> did give <code class=\"notranslate\">//</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to set this comment string in mini.snippet for a specific language  of is this a bug?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.snippets\nQuestion\nHi,\ncurrently I'am trying to migrate from luasnip to mini.snippets. On testing I stumbled upon the issue that LINE_COMMENT for PHP uses the block comment string (/*) in stead of the line comment string (//). see\n:lua print(vim.bo.commentstring:gsub('%s*%%s.*$', ''))\n\nindeed gives /*, but in luasnip LINE_COMMENT did give //.\nIs there a way to set this comment string in mini.snippet for a specific language  of is this a bug?",
